# The canonical file format is LF: `dit fmt` writes `\n`, and the corpus
# round-trip test in dit-parse asserts byte-identity over the markdown files
# checked in here. A Windows clone smudges text files to CRLF by default
# (`core.autocrlf=true` on GitHub's runners), which mutates the corpus before
# any test runs. Pin every text file to LF on checkout so all platforms read
# and write the same bytes; binary files are left untouched by `text=auto`.
* text=auto eol=lf
